. With the legacy of Mahindra for quality and good sales, it is continuing to gain momentum among urban families and adventure lovers. The 3XO also offers some amazing safety features and a fresh design, making it one of the class leaders in the subcompact SUV category. Its robust engineering and premium comfort make it unique among its competitors. Moreover, with a 5-star safety rating in the Bharat NCAP crash tests, the XUV 3XO promises to be a safe and agile car for families every time they drive it. Mahindra XUV 3XO Overview The Mahindra XUV 3XO charms with its aggressive looks, rich interiors, and big cabin space and sets a perfect blend of beauty and comfort with utilitarian value. The sharp LED headlamps, sleek grille, and muscular stance ensure it makes a strong first impression. Inside, the SUV provides a luxurious cabin with exclusive materials, ergonomic seating, and top-notch options for infotainment, assuring an immersive experience for occupants. The XUV 3XO has a host of safety features, such as hill-start assist, electronic stability control, and up to six airbags to ensure driver and passenger safety. Its smooth driving dynamics, excellent manoeuvrability, and strong suspension system ensure a comfortable ride on city roads and rugged terrains. The XUV 3XO comes in various variants, like petrol and diesel, and automatic and manual transmissions to fit the bill for a wide range of customers. Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications The XUV 3XO boasts of its unique design and the highest possible ratings for crash safety. Besides safety, here are the key Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications: Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications Engine 1.2L MPFi Turbo Petrol 1.2L TGDi Turbo Petrol 1.5L Diesel Transmission 6-Speed Manual6-speed TC Automatic 6-Speed ManualAMT Automatic Power 110 PS 130 PS 117 PS Torque 200 Nm 230 Nm 300 Nm Mileage 17.96 km/l 18.20 km/l 21.2 km/l Airbags 6 Airbags as standard Mahindra XUV 3XO Dimensions Length 3990 mm Width 1821 mm Height 1647 mm Wheelbase 