uyers can find value in the Mahindra XUV 3XO due to its pricing arrangement, which spans between 7.99 lakh and 15.57 lakh. Read More: GAME CHANGER: All-New 2025 Mahindra Scorpio with Next-Gen Safety and with BIGGER, BETTER, BOLDER Design! Design Mahindra XUV 3XO has been totally overhauled from its previous model, the XUV300. It now features: Redesigned LED projector headlamps for improved visibility. New LED DRLs will give it a fashionable appearance. A new two-splitted grille and front bumper for a tough appearance. C-shaped LED rear tail lights and full-width LED light bar towards the rear give it a sporty and upscale look in its rear profile. These features give the XUV 3XO a premium and stylish appearance, which is aimed at young customers as well as family buyers. Engine and Performance Three engines come along with the XUV 3XO: 1.2-litre Turbo-Petrol Engine: The engine offers power and torque of 110 bhp and 200 Nm, respectively, and thus delivers a good performance with good fuel efficiency. 1.2-litre Direct Injection Turbo-Petrol Engine: More powerful turbo-petrol motor with 130 bhp power and 230 Nm of torque, perfect for the sportsman driver. 1.5-litre Turbo-Diesel Engine: With 115 bhp and an incredible 300 Nm of torque, this diesel engine is perfect for highway cruising and heavy loads. All the engines are designed to provide a smooth and responsive drive on city streets and highways, too. Features Mahindra XUV 3XO is packed with features that make it the segment leader. Some of the most outstanding of these features are: A 10.25-inch touchscreen infotainment with a natural interface. A 10.25-inch digital instrument cluster with simple access to the majority of driving data. Dual-zone automatic climate control to provide driver and passengers comfort. A panoramic sunroof for a light and fresh interior. A seven-speaker Harman Kardon premium audio system for a luxury listening experience. Wireless Android Auto and Apple CarPlay for easy smartphone integration. All these facets make the XUV 3XO not just a car but a technological marvel as your daily travel companion. Safety Features Safety functions are not among Mahindra's priorities because the XUV 3XO omits all safety standards from its package. It comes with: Level 2 Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS): The XUV 3XO includes Level 2 Advanced Driver Assistance Systems which deliver adaptive cruise control together with lane-keep assist for safer driving operations. 360-degree cameras: The car system shows a complete external panorama that helps during driving operations as well as parking sessions. Six airbags standard: Maximum safety for all on board. Disc brakes, hill descent control, and hill hold control: The system enhances user control thanks to its components, including disc brakes and hill descent control combined with hill hold control, particularly in harsh terrain situations. Traction control: Provides traction on uneven or slippery road surfaces. All safety features\", 'images': [], 'rank': 5}, {'url': 'https://www.carbike360.com/cars/mahindra/xuv-3xo', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 6}, {'url': 'https://automotivemahindra.com/mahindra-xuv-3xo-an-in-depth-specification-breakdown/', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 7}, {'url': 'https://cargraze.com/blog/2025-mahindra-xuv-3xo-specs-design-performance-and-safety', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 8}]",
