ty. With the legacy of Mahindra for quality and good sales, it is continuing to gain momentum among urban families and adventure lovers. The 3XO also offers some amazing safety features and a fresh design, making it one of the class leaders in the subcompact SUV category. Its robust engineering and premium comfort make it unique among its competitors. Moreover, with a 5-star safety rating in the Bharat NCAP crash tests, the XUV 3XO promises to be a safe and agile car for families every time they drive it. Mahindra XUV 3XO Overview The Mahindra XUV 3XO charms with its aggressive looks, rich interiors, and big cabin space and sets a perfect blend of beauty and comfort with utilitarian value. The sharp LED headlamps, sleek grille, and muscular stance ensure it makes a strong first impression. Inside, the SUV provides a luxurious cabin with exclusive materials, ergonomic seating, and top-notch options for infotainment, assuring an immersive experience for occupants. The XUV 3XO has a host of safety features, such as hill-start assist, electronic stability control, and up to six airbags to ensure driver and passenger safety. Its smooth driving dynamics, excellent manoeuvrability, and strong suspension system ensure a comfortable ride on city roads and rugged terrains. The XUV 3XO comes in various variants, like petrol and diesel, and automatic and manual transmissions to fit the bill for a wide range of customers. Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications The XUV 3XO boasts of its unique design and the highest possible ratings for crash safety. Besides safety, here are the key Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications: Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications Engine 1.2L MPFi Turbo Petrol 1.2L TGDi Turbo Petrol 1.5L Diesel Transmission 6-Speed Manual6-speed TC Automatic 6-Speed ManualAMT Automatic Power 110 PS 130 PS 117 PS Torque 200 Nm 230 Nm 300 Nm Mileage 17.96 km/l 18.20 km/l 21.2 km/l Airbags 6 Airbags as standard Mahindra XUV 3XO Dimensions Length 3990 mm Width 1821 mm Height 1647 mm Wheelbase 2600 mm Boot Space 295 litres Mahindra XUV 3XO Safety Features Airbags 6 Standard ABS with EBD Standard Rear Parking Sensors Standard All Wheel Disc Brakes Standard Reverse Parking Camera Higher Variants Electronic Stability Programme Standard Tyre Pressure Monitoring System Higher Variants ISOFIX Mounts Standard Hill Hold Assist Standard Hill Descent Control Standard Mahindra XUV 3XO Feature Highlights Dual-Zone Automatic Climate Control AX5 and above Sunroof AX7 and above Front Parking Sensors Standard Mahindra XUV 3XO Price The Mahindra XUV 3XO price offers great value for money, catering to various budgets. The price\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://ackodrive.com/car-guide/mahindra-xuv-3xo-features-explained/', 'content': 'Mahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: Your Complete Guide Home / Articles / Car Guide / Mahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: A Comprehensive Guide. Mahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: A Comprehensive Guide. Published on 27 Aug, 2024, 9:41 AM IST Updated on 28 Aug, 2024, 5:59 AM IST Team Ackodrive 8 min read Interesting Articles Follow us on Share Post Mahindra recently launched the much-awaited Mahindra XUV 3XO as a compact SUV in the Indian automotive industry. Outperforming its rivals, the Tata Nexon, Hyundai Venue and Maruti Suzuki Brezza, the Mahindra XUV 3XO brings a fresh look to the segment. With the latest updates and comfortable features, the Mahindra XUV 3XO is on the list of must-buy compact SUVs in India. Here, we will take a closer look at the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained and help you choose the ideal car. Contents Price of Mahindra XUV 3XO Variants After the Mahindra XUV 3XO features are explained, you must know the price of each variant. Hence, we have prepared a table for you highlighting the ex-showroom price of each XUV 3XO variant: Mahindra XUV 3XO Variant Ex-Showroom Price MX1 Rs. 7.49 Lakhs MX2 Rs. 9.99 Lakhs MX2 PRO Rs. 8.99 Lakhs to Rs. 10.39 Lakhs MX3 Rs. 9.49 Lakhs to Rs. 11.68 Lakhs MX3 PRO Rs. 9.99 Lakhs to Rs. 11.49 Lakhs AX5 Rs. 10.69 Lakhs to Rs. 12.88 Lakhs AX5 Luxury Rs. 11.99 Lakhs to Rs. 13.49 Lakhs AX7 Rs. 12.49 Lakhs to Rs. 14.49 Lakhs AX7 Luxury Rs. 13.99 Lakhs to Rs. 15.49 Lakhs Note : The prices of the Mahindra XUV 3XO variants can change without any prior notice. So, before booking your car, talk with your nearest dealer to know the latest price. Check out: Mahindra XUV 3XO Variants Unlatch Elated Driving Experience with the All New Mahindra XUV 3XO Making its presence felt in the Indian compact SUV market, the Mahindra XUV 3XO is one of the best cars in this segment manufactured by Mahindra. It offers more convenience and comfort when driving on different terrains. The following are detailed discussions of the Mahindra XUV 3XO tech specs and features: 1. Influencing Exterior Look The Mahindra XUV 3XO has a specific design to turn heads with its athletic stance. It commands respect and exudes the confidence of a true SUV. The all-new Mahindra XUV 3XO has an ample ground clearance of 201 mm, making it easy for you to drive on rocky terrains. In addition, the XUV 3XO comes with a command seating position to offer an exhilarating driving experience. The Mahindra XUV 3XO has LED DRLs and headlamps that will lead the road to envy you whenever you turn them on. Furthermore, the infinity tail lamps add an X factor to your style quotient. The car also features 17-inch diamond-cut alloy wheels for that sporty look. Check out: Mahindra XUV 3XO Dimensions 2. Comforting Interior When you drive the Mahindra XUV 3XO, it elevates your every journey. Stepping inside the XUV 3XOs cabin will let you discover a sanctuary of sophistication and comfort. It is one of the key parts of the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained, as it has a meticulous design for the finest SUV lovers. The Mahindra XUV 3XO features a Skyroof and soft-touch leatherette on the door trims and dashboard. Furthermore, the car has premium leatherette seats, a cooled glovebox with illumination, and a passive keyless entry. It also features a front armrest with storage and a console with a cup holder for a comfortable drive. Check out: Mahindra XUV 3XO Interior 3. Smart Connectivity Another key Mahindra XUV 3XO configuration is its smart connectivity and technology. The car comes with a Harman Kardon 7-speaker audio system to make your drive enjoyable. In addition, the sound system lets you experience sonic expanse, and the bass enhancer technology uplifts your mood while driving in crowded areas. The Mahindra XUV 3XO features a high-definition touchscreen system for infotainment and navigation and has built-in Amazon Alexa for entertainment. Moreover, with the ADRENOX Connect technology, you can control your cars features through y', 'images': [], 'rank': 3}, {'url': 'https://www.cardekho.com/mahindra/xuv-3xo/specs', 'content': \"Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications - Dimensions, Configurations, Features, Engine cc All New Used English Login / Register NEW CARS Explore New Cars Electric Cars Tata Harrier EV Mahindra XEV 9e Mahindra BE 6 MG Windsor EV MG Comet EV Tata Nexon EV All Electric Cars Popular Cars Defender Mahindra XUV 3XO Hyundai Creta Mahindra Scorpio Mahindra Thar ROXX Mahindra XUV700 All Popular Cars Upcoming Cars New Launches Car Insurance Ad Popular Brands Maruti Cars Tata Cars Kia Cars Toyota Cars Hyundai Cars Mahindra Cars Compare Cars New Car Offers & Discounts Find Car Dealers Find EV Charging Stations Find Fuel Stations Check Fuel Prices Used cars Buy Used Cars Used Cars In Your City Ahmedabad Bangalore Chennai Delhi NCR Hyderabad Jaipur Kolkata Mumbai Pune More Cities Sell My Car Used Car Valuation Dealership Near Me News & Reviews News & Top stories Car Expert Reviews User Reviews Car Collection Tips & Advice Videos Video Reviews Visual Stories Select City Ad XUV 3XO Price Compare Images Specs User Reviews 360 View Variants Videos More Mileage Colours XUV 3XO News FAQs Dealers Service Center Brochure XUV 3XO EMI Loan Second Hand XUV 3XO Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications The Mahindra XUV 3XO has 1 Diesel Engine and 1 Petrol Engine on offer. The Diesel engine is 1498 cc while the Petrol engine is 1197 cc . It is available with Manual & Automatic transmission.Depending upon the variant and fuel type the XUV 3XO has a mileage of 17.96 to 20.6 kmpl. The XUV 3XO is a 5 seater 3 cylinder car and has length of 3990 mm, width of 1821 mm and a wheelbase of 2600. Read More 4.6 302 Reviews Shortlist Rs. 7.99 - 15.80 Lakh * EMI starts @ 21,646 View July Offers Ad Standout features of Mahindra XUV 3XO Soft touch material on dashboard and door pads. Panoramic sunroof - largest in the segment. Level 2 ADAS with features such as forward collision warning, adaptive cruise control. 1.2-litre turbo-petrol engine makes 130PS/230Nm most powerful in its class. Key specifications of Mahindra XUV 3XO ARAI Mileage 18.2 kmpl Fuel Type Petrol Engine Displacement 1197 cc No. of Cylinders 3 Max Power 128.73bhp@5000rpm Max Torque 230Nm@1500-3750rpm Seating Capacity 5 Transmission Type Automatic Boot Space 364 Litres Fuel Tank Capacity 42 Litres Body Type SUV Key features of Mahindra XUV 3XO Power Steering Yes Power Windows Front Yes Anti-lock Braking System (ABS) Yes Air Conditioner Yes Driver Airbag Yes Passenger Airbag Yes Automatic Climate Control Yes Alloy Wheels Yes Multi-function Steering Wheel Yes Mahindra XUV 3XO specifications Engine & Transmission Engine Type mStallion (TGDi) engine Displacement 1197 cc Max Power 128.73bhp@5000rpm Max Torque 230Nm@1500-3750rpm No. of Cylinders 3 Valves Per Cylinder 4 Turbo Charger Yes Transmission Type Automatic Gearbox 6-Speed AT Drive Type FWD Report Incorrect Specs Don't miss out on the best offers for this Month View July Offers Fuel & Performance Fuel Type Petrol Petrol Mileage ARAI 18.2 kmpl Petrol Fuel Tank Capacity 42 Litres Emission Norm Compliance BS VI 2.0 Report Incorrect Specs Suspension, Steering & Brakes Front Suspension MacPherson Strut suspension Rear Suspension Rear twist beam Steering Type Electric Turning Radius 5.3 m Front Brake Type Disc Rear Brake Type Disc Alloy Wheel Size Front 17 Inch Alloy Wheel Size Rear 17 Inch Report Incorrect Specs Don't miss out on the best offers for this Month View July Offers Dimensions & Capacity Length 3990 mm Width 1821 mm Height 1647 mm Boot Space 364 Litres Seating Capacity 5 Wheel Base 2600 mm No. of Doors 5 Report Incorrect Specs Don't miss out on the best offers for this Month View July Offers Comfort & Convenience Power Steering Air Conditioner Heater Height Adjustable Driver Seat Ventilated Seats Electric Adjustable Seats Automatic Climate Control Accessory Power Outlet Rear Reading Lamp Adjustable Headrest Rear Seat Centre Arm Rest Height Adjustable Front Seat Belts Rear AC Vents Cruise Control Parking Sensors Front & Rear Real-Time Vehicle Tracking Foldabl\", 'images': [], 'rank': 4}, {'url': 'https://www.carversal.com/blogs/mahindra-xuv-3xo-onroad-price-features--specs--full-details/520', 'content': \"Mahindra XUV 3XO On-Road Price, Features & Specs | Full Details CARVERSAL Home About Us Contact Us Privacy Policy More Login Term and Conditions Disclosure Home About Us Privacy Policy Contact Us More Login Term and Conditions Disclosure Mahindra XUV 3XO On-Road Price, Features & Specs | Full Details March 12th, 2025 Mahindra XUV 3XO is the latest compact SUV from Mahindra that is trying to make its presence felt strongly in the Indian market. With a price of between 7.49 lakh (ex-showroom) for the lowest variant and 15.49 lakh for the highest variant, the XUV 3XO has sufficient variants to provide to the buyers. It comes in nine trims and 25 variants in total, so there is something for everyone. Let us look more at the Mahindra XUV 3XO's On Road price and features. Mahindra XUV 3XO Price At 7.99 lakh, the Mahindra XUV 3XO begins its price range from its base model. The fully stocked top model of the Mahindra XUV 3XO comes with a price tag reaching up to 15.57 lakh on average. Different buyers can find value in the Mahindra XUV 3XO due to its pricing arrangement, which spans between 7.99 lakh and 15.57 lakh. Read More: GAME CHANGER: All-New 2025 Mahindra Scorpio with Next-Gen Safety and with BIGGER, BETTER, BOLDER Design! Design Mahindra XUV 3XO has been totally overhauled from its previous model, the XUV300. It now features: Redesigned LED projector headlamps for improved visibility. New LED DRLs will give it a fashionable appearance. A new two-splitted grille and front bumper for a tough appearance. C-shaped LED rear tail lights and full-width LED light bar towards the rear give it a sporty and upscale look in its rear profile. These features give the XUV 3XO a premium and stylish appearance, which is aimed at young customers as well as family buyers. Engine and Performance Three engines come along with the XUV 3XO: 1.2-litre Turbo-Petrol Engine: The engine offers power and torque of 110 bhp and 200 Nm, respectively, and thus delivers a good performance with good fuel efficiency. 1.2-litre Direct Injection Turbo-Petrol Engine: More powerful turbo-petrol motor with 130 bhp power and 230 Nm of torque, perfect for the sportsman driver. 1.5-litre Turbo-Diesel Engine: With 115 bhp and an incredible 300 Nm of torque, this diesel engine is perfect for highway cruising and heavy loads. All the engines are designed to provide a smooth and responsive drive on city streets and highways, too. Features Mahindra XUV 3XO is packed with features that make it the segment leader. Some of the most outstanding of these features are: A 10.25-inch touchscreen infotainment with a natural interface. A 10.25-inch digital instrument cluster with simple access to the majority of driving data. Dual-zone automatic climate control to provide driver and passengers comfort. A panoramic sunroof for a light and fresh interior. A seven-speaker Harman Kardon premium audio system for a luxury listening experience. Wireless Android Auto and Apple CarPlay for easy smartphone integration. All these facets make the XUV 3XO not just a car but a technological marvel as your daily travel companion. Safety Features Safety functions are not among Mahindra's priorities because the XUV 3XO omits all safety standards from its package. It comes with: Level 2 Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS): The XUV 3XO includes Level 2 Advanced Driver Assistance Systems which deliver adaptive cruise control together with lane-keep assist for safer driving operations. 360-degree cameras: The car system shows a complete external panorama that helps during driving operations as well as parking sessions. Six airbags standard: Maximum safety for all on board. Disc brakes, hill descent control, and hill hold control: The system enhances user control thanks to its components, including disc brakes and hill descent control combined with hill hold control, particularly in harsh terrain situations. Traction control: Provides traction on uneven or slippery road surfaces. All safety features\", 'images': [], 'rank': 5}, {'url': 'https://www.carbike360.com/cars/mahindra/xuv-3xo', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 6}, {'url': 'https://automotivemahindra.com/mahindra-xuv-3xo-an-in-depth-specification-breakdown/', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 7}, {'url': 'https://cargraze.com/blog/2025-mahindra-xuv-3xo-specs-design-performance-and-safety', 'content': '[not extracted] Content limit reached', 'rank': 8}]",
